    },
    {
      "id": "dEGXeuOMEdEFH1pS8GTp6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -752.5942549497368,
      "y": 5784.875365101908,
      "width": 990.478271484375,
      "height": 1225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "am",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 298458235,
      "version": 226,
      "versionNonce": 1971358267,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791388516726,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "BERT — 2018\nIntroduced bidirectional Transformer encoders pretrained with Masked Language Modeling (MLM) and\nNext Sentence Prediction (NSP).\n\nmBERT — 2018\nExtended BERT to 104 languages using a shared multilingual vocabulary, enabling cross-lingual\ntransfer within a single encoder.\n\nRoBERTa — 2019\nImproved BERT through better pretraining: more data, longer training, larger batches, dynamic\nmasking, and removal of NSP.\n\nDistilBERT — 2019\nUsed knowledge distillation to create a smaller, faster version of BERT while preserving most of its\nperformance.\n\nALBERT — 2019\nReduced parameter count through factorized embeddings and cross-layer parameter sharing;\nintroduced Sentence Order Prediction.\n\nXLM — 2019\nIntroduced cross-lingual pretraining objectives, including the use of parallel corpora to align\nrepresentations across languages.\n\nXLM-RoBERTa — 2019\nCombined RoBERTa-style training with large-scale multilingual pretraining across 100 languages,\nsubstantially improving multilingual encoder performance.\n\nELECTRA — 2020\nReplaced masked-token prediction with Replaced Token Detection, making pretraining more\ncomputationally efficient.\n\nMobileBERT — 2020\nOptimized the BERT architecture for mobile and resource-constrained environments, reducing model\nsize and inference cost.\n\nDeBERTa — 2020\nIntroduced disentangled attention, modeling token content and positional information separately.\n\nDeBERTa-v3 — 2021\nCombined DeBERTa's disentangled attention with an ELECTRA-style pretraining objective, improving\nboth efficiency and performance.\n\nmDeBERTa / multilingual DeBERTa — 2021 onward\nExtended DeBERTa-style architectural improvements to multilingual representation learning.\n\nModernBERT — 2024\nModernized the BERT paradigm with RoPE, FlashAttention, local/global attention, an 8K context\nwindow, and large-scale pretraining, while preserving the bidirectional encoder-only architecture.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "BERT — 2018\nIntroduced bidirectional Transformer encoders pretrained with Masked Language Modeling (MLM) and Next Sentence Prediction (NSP).\n\nmBERT — 2018\nExtended BERT to 104 languages using a shared multilingual vocabulary, enabling cross-lingual transfer within a single encoder.\n\nRoBERTa — 2019\nImproved BERT through better pretraining: more data, longer training, larger batches, dynamic masking, and removal of NSP.\n\nDistilBERT — 2019\nUsed knowledge distillation to create a smaller, faster version of BERT while preserving most of its performance.\n\nALBERT — 2019\nReduced parameter count through factorized embeddings and cross-layer parameter sharing; introduced Sentence Order Prediction.\n\nXLM — 2019\nIntroduced cross-lingual pretraining objectives, including the use of parallel corpora to align representations across languages.\n\nXLM-RoBERTa — 2019\nCombined RoBERTa-style training with large-scale multilingual pretraining across 100 languages, substantially improving multilingual encoder performance.\n\nELECTRA — 2020\nReplaced masked-token prediction with Replaced Token Detection, making pretraining more computationally efficient.\n\nMobileBERT — 2020\nOptimized the BERT architecture for mobile and resource-constrained environments, reducing model size and inference cost.\n\nDeBERTa — 2020\nIntroduced disentangled attention, modeling token content and positional information separately.\n\nDeBERTa-v3 — 2021\nCombined DeBERTa's disentangled attention with an ELECTRA-style pretraining objective, improving both efficiency and performance.\n\nmDeBERTa / multilingual DeBERTa — 2021 onward\nExtended DeBERTa-style architectural improvements to multilingual representation learning.\n\nModernBERT — 2024\nModernized the BERT paradigm with RoPE, FlashAttention, local/global attention, an 8K context window, and large-scale pretraining, while preserving the bidirectional encoder-only architecture.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "7OGR8bf9wM1AXrEqvT855",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -377.09072405005236,
      "y": 7157.758397892727,
      "width": 190.58404541015625,
      "height": 41.4,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "o49aWYPbEeQuKXRpRregJ",
        "IOUfhrgnHRvNLolE0eKsj"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "an",
