      "updated": 1791388738357,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Italian BERT",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Italian BERT",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
    {
      "id": "CCXugKatROFU0ddW4wePw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -754.6291660259644,
      "y": 7231.791731226059,
      "width": 990.478271484375,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "IOUfhrgnHRvNLolE0eKsj"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ao",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 835203867,
      "version": 313,
      "versionNonce": 1499663637,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791388738357,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Italian models were released in 2020 by the MDZ Digital Library team (dbmdz) at the Bavarian\nState Library — Bayerische Staatsbibliothek (BSB), Munich., which has published a collection of\npretrained language models on Hugging Face. Their Italian family includes both BERT and ELECTRA\nmodels. Hugging Face\n\nbert-base-italian-cased / uncased\nThese models keep the standard BERT-base architecture, but they are pretrained specifically on\nItalian. The training corpus combines an Italian Wikipedia dump with texts from the OPUS corpora,\nfor a total of about 13 GB and 2.05 billion tokens. Hugging Face\nThe main idea is straightforward: same BERT architecture, but vocabulary and representations\nspecialized for Italian.\n\nbert-base-italian-xxl-cased / uncased\nThe XXL versions use the same BERT-base architecture but are pretrained on a substantially larger\nItalian corpus. The original OPUS/Wikipedia data is extended with the Italian portion of OSCAR,\nbringing the training corpus to approximately 81 GB and 13.1 billion tokens. Hugging Face\nSo XXL does not mean a larger Transformer architecture here. It mainly refers to the much larger\npretraining dataset.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Italian models were released in 2020 by the MDZ Digital Library team (dbmdz) at the Bavarian State Library — Bayerische Staatsbibliothek (BSB), Munich., which has published a collection of pretrained language models on Hugging Face. Their Italian family includes both BERT and ELECTRA models. Hugging Face\n\nbert-base-italian-cased / uncased\nThese models keep the standard BERT-base architecture, but they are pretrained specifically on Italian. The training corpus combines an Italian Wikipedia dump with texts from the OPUS corpora, for a total of about 13 GB and 2.05 billion tokens. Hugging Face\nThe main idea is straightforward: same BERT architecture, but vocabulary and representations specialized for Italian.\n\nbert-base-italian-xxl-cased / uncased\nThe XXL versions use the same BERT-base architecture but are pretrained on a substantially larger Italian corpus. The original OPUS/Wikipedia data is extended with the Italian portion of OSCAR, bringing the training corpus to approximately 81 GB and 13.1 billion tokens. Hugging Face\nSo XXL does not mean a larger Transformer architecture here. It mainly refers to the much larger pretraining dataset.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
